 "briefing": "# Databricks Meeting Briefing: 17 November 2026\n\n## Research Status\n\nNo verified Databricks developments could be confirmed for the window of 16 October to 15 November 2026. Every search attempt returned a rate-limit error, and the page-fetch attempts did not return content. As a result, no news items, product launches, hires, or deals are listed below. Nothing has been filled in from memory or from older coverage.\n\nBefore the meeting, the primary sources listed under Sources should be checked directly, since they are the most likely to show in-window activity.\n\n## News\n\nNo dated news items from the window were verified. Any item presented as recent news should be checked against the Databricks newsroom and the blog before it is raised in the meeting.\n\n## Product Launches\n\nNo product announcements, general availability releases, previews, or platform updates dated within the window were verified. Release notes and the blog are the fastest way to confirm launches for specific product lines, such as the Data Intelligence Platform, Lakebase, Agent Bricks, Genie, and Unity Catalog.\n\n## Executive and Notable Hires\n\nNo executive appointments, departures, board changes, or other notable hires dated within the window were verified. The leadership and careers pages should be checked for changes after 16 October 2026.\n\n## Deals\n\nNo acquisitions, partnerships, funding rounds, valuation changes, customer wins, or other commercial agreements dated within the window were verified. Databricks' SEC EDGAR record should be checked for any filings, and the newsroom and partner press releases should be checked for announcements.\n\n## Open Questions for the Meeting\n\nThese questions are general and are not based on verified in-window findings. They should be confirmed against the primary sources before the meeting.\n\n1. Which product announcements from the past month should we treat as priorities for our roadmap, and what are their availability dates?\n2. Have there been any changes to the leadership team or to the teams that own our account, and who is our main point of contact going forward?\n3. Are there any new partnerships, commercial terms, or customer programs that would affect our pricing or contract options in the coming quarter?\n\n## Sources\n\n[1] Databricks Newsroom (primary source to check, not verified for window): https://www.databricks.com/company/newsroom\n[2] Databricks Blog (primary source to check, not verified for window): https://www.databricks.com/blog\n[3] Databricks Leadership Page (primary source to check, not verified for window): https://www.databricks.com/company/leadership\n[4] Databricks Release Notes (primary source to check, not verified for window): https://docs.databricks.com/aws/en/release-notes/\n[5] SEC EDGAR Company Search (primary source to check for any filings): https://www.sec.gov/edgar/search/",
